/**
 * athanorWikiParts.js — THE PARTS REFERENCE of the Athanor's wiki: one entry per part.
 *
 *   A page for every part:
 *   what goes in, what comes out,
 *   and what each dial does.
 *
 * Ruby: the Athanor's help should teach someone who has never used a node editor how these systems
 * work — informative, approachable, technically correct (Filter Forge's help is the model). Each
 * entry: line (the one sentence shown in the parts list and menus), about (the article's opening),
 * ins / outs (by port name) and set (by setting key) explaining each, tips (things to try), see
 * (related articles: 'part:key' or an article id). Ports and settings left out are listed with their
 * kind and range only. The article is put together in athanorWiki.js.
 */
